  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Assessing Firebase Readiness**\n\nI\'ve got `firebase.ts` squared away. Now I\'m shifting gears to a broader repository scan, identifying the remaining puzzle pieces. My focus is on the architecture, determining which files are critical for the forthcoming user request handling functionality, and how to start building the requested multi-section generation component.\n\n\n**Re-evaluating R3F Dependency**\n\nI\'m reconsidering the initial R3F recommendation for the interactive 3D sphere. Weighing its potential installation complexities and size, I\'m exploring alternatives. Can a polished Canvas-based particle sphere, or a dynamic SVG/CSS/Canvas solution deliver a similar holographic core experience, while reducing dependencies? The \"glowing, rotatable AI Core sphere reacting to cursor movement\" is the key. My focus is on achieving this with minimal overhead.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Canvas Solution**\n\nI\'ve made a firm decision: the HTML5 `<canvas>` approach is the way to go. The potential React 19 and `@react-three/fiber` conflicts are a non-starter. This custom canvas sphere is 100% stable, and simpler. I\'m excited about developing this custom component!\n\n\n**Defining Core Requirements**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on defining core UI/UX requirements. The interactive holographic particle sphere, rendered through canvas, is the centerpiece. My focus is the navigation and hero section. I\'m carefully analyzing the page structure, especially the \"Floating Glass Island\" navbar and the cinematic Hero section to ensure the canvas sphere fits in with the intended aesthetic. The goal is to build the interactive features, including the dynamic logo, the navigation links, and the call-to-action buttons.\n\n\n**Designing Demo Engine**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the \"Interactive Live Demo Engine.\" My focus is on the crucial client-side scanner interface and its Firebase connection. I\'m prioritizing the drag-and-drop/camera capture functionality and the visual logs for a multi-step loading state. I\'m also planning the Verification Result Dashboard, including an authenticity score radial gauge and a fraud risk heatmap with bounding box visualizer. This is all integrated with Firebase for scan report auto-saving and generating shareable links. I will be working on the primary CTA buttons: \"Try Live Demo\" and \"Watch Vision Architecture\".\n\n\n**Designing Node Flow**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing the interactive \"Vision Architecture\" flow diagram, a key component of my vision. I\'m building an interactive node system visualizing the AI pipeline. Each node will trigger a glass drawer revealing detailed model parameters. I\'ll also add an \"Interactive Feature Matrix\" to contrast TruthScan AI with traditional verification methods using liquid-glass comparison cards. The goal is to make it super compelling and clear.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 173515078
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
