  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the Demo Engine**\n\nI\'ve got the waitlist modal wrapped up! It\'s fully connected to Firestore, dynamically prioritizing entries, firing off confetti, and handling errors seamlessly. I\'m now turning my attention to designing the Interactive Live Demo Engine, focusing on how Firebase Storage and AI simulation will work together.\n\n\n**Defining the Sample Images**\n\nI\'m solidifying the user flow for the demo. They\'ll have three sample images: a serum, lip gloss, and perfume, each with mock packaging overlays, giving a detailed visual playground. They\'ll also be able to upload their own images, with a client-side parser simulating a server-side analysis. The output will be an authenticity score, bounding box, fraud heatmap, and a Firestore-saved report with a shareable link.\n\n\n**Crafting the Example Data**\n\nI\'m now generating specific example product data to showcase the demo\'s capabilities. I\'m focusing on two scenarios: a genuine \"Molecular Renewal Elixir\" with a high authenticity score and a counterfeit \"Hydra-Lustre Gloss\" with a low score. Each will include detailed log entries to illustrate the analysis process, along with visually appealing descriptions for both products to highlight the features of the AI model. I\'m choosing brands and products, and I am describing the image content.\n\n\n**Developing the UI Scanner**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the user interface for the live demo scanner component, `/src/components/LiveScanner.tsx`. It will feature preset image selections and a custom image upload option. A real-time moving laser grid line will overlay the image, alongside AI simulation features, including bounding boxes, labels, and real-time authenticity scoring. The results will auto-save to Firestore, updating the user\'s historical scan list.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 50
      nanos: 48839713
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
